Crabmon, it's working.

112
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:48,537
Why don't you show these guys how
we take care of things down under?

113
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:51,679
I kind of like the rice
part, but let's spice it up.

114
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:52,990
Champalaya!

115
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:55,084
Please don't leave me for that!

116
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:05,277
And when we're done, we're going to make
you into our favorite dessert, brownie!

117
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,420
Ice cream. Pie!

118
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:10,391
They're headed for the Great Barrier Reef.

119
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:11,991
Hang on tight, everybody.

120
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:19,177
Joe, you're looking a little green.

121
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:20,090
Are you okay?

122
00:06:20,173 --> 00:06:21,617
I'm feeling a bit seasick.

123
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:24,935
Fortunately, it only happens
whenever I'm around water.

124
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,660
There it is!

125
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:28,300
The Great Barrier Reef!

126
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:30,020
And look over there!

127
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:31,760
The last control spire!

128
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:36,380
You worry about those three later.

129
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:39,688
First, we have to destroy
the control spire.

130
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,430
Yeah!

131
00:06:41,513 --> 00:06:42,343
Ikkakumon, let him go!

132
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:45,180
Whoa, that was too close!

133
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:48,457
With all this talk about
food, I'm getting hungry.

134
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:50,658
What do you say we all go out for...

135
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:55,408
First, you have to get
past me, Scorpio-mon.

136
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:59,920
I'll handle this low-life,
penny-pinchin' arachnid.

137
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:04,720
No one calls me arachnid.

138
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,233
He's too strong for us.

139
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,520
Ikkakumon, you've got to digivolve.

140
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,060
Digimon, digivolve.

141
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,132
Ikkakumon, digivolve too!

142
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,504
Digimon, know to the champions.

143
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:43,937
They're destroying all
the coral in the reef.

144
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:47,417
We have to do something if we
let them keep fighting like this.

145
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:50,060
The entire barrier reef will be wiped out.

146
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,534
Pseudomon, underwater.

147
00:07:56,060 --> 00:07:58,957
Yeah, when it comes to
water, you know what to do.

148
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:00,158
Now you're talking.

149
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:07,000
Armadimon, armor digivolve to...

150
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,120
Crabmon, it's your turn.

151
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:29,264
Crabmon, Crabmon, Crabmon, too!

152
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:32,750
Golemon!

153
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:37,361
That's Golemon.

154
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:41,077
If you thought Crabmon was crappy, where
do you see this guy's fossil blight attack?

155
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:43,817
He'll wipe out his enemy's
hook, line, and sinker.

156
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:48,117
Submarimon, we have to find a way to lead
Scorpio-mon away from the coral reef!

157
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,030
You've got it!

158
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:02,400
Oxygen! Torpedo!

159
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:10,417
I don't know how to get him to follow me!

160
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:13,740
Erachnid! Erachnid! Erachnid!

161
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:19,880
Vulcan's Hammer!

162
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:25,320
Oxygen Torpedo!

163
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:35,400
Wow, he's out cold.

164
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:36,977
Maybe our attack was too strong.

165
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:37,940
He'll be okay.

166
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:40,380
I think he just fainted.

167
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:43,290
Yay!

168
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:45,997
Now we can finally
destroy the Control Spire.

169
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:48,157
All right, I'm going to take
a shot at the base of it.

170
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:50,477
Submarimon, I want you
to attack from the side.

171
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:52,820
Then we can get that fossil bite!

172
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:57,116
That will work, too!

173
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:15,797
The other Digidestined have
lived the Digimon right to us.

174
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:18,797
We can send them all home and be
back in time for the barbecue.

175
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:19,720
Good on you.

176
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,937
Do you think they'll have something mild?

177
00:10:22,020 --> 00:10:23,549
My stomach's still queasy.

178
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,280
Okay, Digi-port, open.

179
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:34,777
Hey, Derek, I've got another question.

180
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:36,257
Why do they call it Down Under?

181
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:38,164
It's not really under anything.

182
00:10:56,780 --> 00:10:58,597
Wow, check out the Eiffel Tower.

183
00:10:58,680 --> 00:11:00,797
That's got to be the world's
tallest Christmas tree.

184
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:01,710
Yeah,

185
00:11:01,793 --> 00:11:04,217
and I'd love to stand around and look at
the decorations on the Arc de Triomphe,

186
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,397
but I've got two problems.

187
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:07,951
One, we've got to find the control spires.

188
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,940
And two, I'm freezing out here. TK,

189
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:12,597
you told me your grandfather, Michel,

190
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:14,997
lives here in Paris and would
be willing to lend us a hand.

191
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,160
So where is he?

192
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:19,297
Listen, Tai, if my grandfather
says he's going to do something,

193
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:21,637
well, eight times out of
ten, he's going to do it.

194
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,617
What if this is one of
the other two times?

195
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:27,217
We don't know our way around Paris and
neither one of us speaks any French.

196
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:31,217
I told him this time it was an
emergency, so don't worry, he'll be here.

197
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:32,130
Ah!

198
00:11:32,213 --> 00:11:33,857
Uh-oh, here comes one of those biker guys.

199
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:35,820
And he looks pretty mean, too.

200
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:41,530
TK!

201
00:11:41,613 --> 00:11:42,680
Grandpa, hey!

202
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:45,674
Are you ready to sing?

203
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:47,020
What do you mean?

204
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:50,497
You know you have to sing Fleur
de Jacques every time you see me.

205
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:52,457
Grandpa, the world's in a lot of danger.

206
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:53,370
He's right.

207
00:11:53,453 --> 00:11:54,717
The future of Earth depends on us.

208
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:56,377
There's no time for singing.

209
00:11:56,460 --> 00:11:59,578
Danger or no danger, there's
always time for singing.

210
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:04,257
Hey, Grandpa, why didn't
you bring Grandma?

211
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:07,517
She was finishing up some
plumbing work in the kitchen.

212
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:12,188
Anyway, whenever we go for a ride on
this ding, she always insists on driving.

213
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:13,320
I understand.

214
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:15,910
Besides,

215
00:12:15,993 --> 00:12:19,457
I have a strange feeling things are
going to get a little rough here tonight.

216
00:12:19,540 --> 00:12:21,757
This calls for somewhat
tough and dominating.

217
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,757
Sounds to me like she's right for the job.

218
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:28,546
I don't really care who it is as long as
we find and destroy the control spires.

219
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:32,117
This wasn't how I was planning
to spend my Christmas Eve.

220
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,057
I know, Grandpa.

221
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:35,669
If all goes well, when
we wake up tomorrow,

222
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:37,437
it'll be just as if nothing ever happened.

223
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:39,437
A nice, peaceful Christmas morning.

224
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:40,461
Not at my house.

225
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:42,937
Grandma's putting up a new roof tomorrow.

226
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:43,940
Hang on tight.

227
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:46,120
She adjusted the brakes last week.

228
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:49,089
Why did you stop, Grandpa?

229
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,060
Something is not right here.

230
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:53,530
Huh?

231
00:12:53,613 --> 00:12:54,443
What is it?

232
00:12:55,620 --> 00:12:57,397
It's the gate to Versailles Palace.

233
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:58,480
She is wide open.

234
00:12:58,820 --> 00:12:59,761
And look inside.

235
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:01,737
There are no guards and she's all lit up.

236
00:13:01,820 --> 00:13:03,500
What's going on? So what?

237
00:13:03,640 --> 00:13:06,537
It's probably being used for one
of those secret celebrity weddings.

238
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:07,450
No!

239
00:13:07,533 --> 00:13:10,137
This is not one of those rental
halls that serves rubber chicken.

240
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:11,050
I'm sorry.

241
00:13:11,133 --> 00:13:12,057
I didn't mean anything by it.

242
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:13,552
It was just a joke, sir.

243
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:14,980
I'm not laughing.

244
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:17,360
Grandpa, come on, let's get going.

245
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:20,897
It's my responsibility as a Frenchman to
investigate the matter and if need be,

246
00:13:20,980 --> 00:13:21,810
to act on it.

247
00:13:21,893 --> 00:13:22,723
So it's open.

248
00:13:22,806 --> 00:13:23,636
What's the big deal?

249
00:13:23,719 --> 00:13:25,237
The most important
thing to the French is a

250
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:27,877
good bakery and the second
is Versailles Palace.

251
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:28,842
Vive la France!

252
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,877
Wait, but what am I
supposed to tell Grandma?

253
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:32,240
Are you kidding?

254
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:34,197
If she saw this gate was left unattended,

255
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,817
she would have someone's
head on a platter.

256
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:38,617
Whenever the gate needs repairs,
who do you think they call?

257
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:40,160
Let's go! Wait up!

